Subject: Tweak: CPU vs CPU
Upstream-base: 7a6bf165d9f1c5914181c079c7d4bfa7204f3509

Choose Sides offers its Done button only while a controller is on a side:
UpdateHomeAwayVisibility shows Done for the first one, and hides and disables
it again when the last one leaves. With "CPU vs CPU" enabled, Done stays
available with no controller on a side in offline Domination, on its Choose
Sides screen and on the pause menu's. Proceed then stores no side for any pad,
and the CPU plays both teams, as in the title screen's demo matches
(StartDemoMatch resets every pad's side). Any controller can still pause. The
Road to the Striker Cup, Strikers 101, the Striker Challenges and online or LAN
matches keep the original rule.

Issue #31's Gecko code got there by never drawing Done: SetButtonVisibility
stored false for it, so the branch that hides and disables Done, which tests
whether it is drawn, never ran.

